From b1482e1e1590306027ebf5ebd6d7df1ceab84ec5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Glathe <jens.glathe@oldschoolsolutions.biz>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:07:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_pas: set RPROC_DETACHED for non-PAS
 path

When the non-PAS (attach-only) path is selected, mark the remoteproc
RPROC_DETACHED before rproc_add(). This tells the remoteproc core that
the remote is already running and should only be attached to, rather
than treated as offline and potentially subject to start or recovery
logic that assumes a full boot path is available.

Co-developed-by: Val Packett <val@packett.cool>
Signed-off-by: Jens Glathe <jens.glathe@oldschoolsolutions.biz>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
index e7b1366..813fa78 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -1036,7 +1036,7 @@ static int qcom_pas_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			pas->dtb_pas_ctx->use_tzmem = desc->needs_tzmem || rproc->has_iommu;
 	}
 
-	if (desc->early_boot)
+	if (desc->early_boot || !use_pas)
 		pas->rproc->state = RPROC_DETACHED;
 
 	ret = rproc_add(rproc);
-- 
2.53.0

